{
  "about": [
    "Deadline parsing, labels and tones. Implementations: worker/public/js/dates.js (parseDue, dueLabel, dueTone) and",
    "desktop/rules.ps1 (Parse-Due, Due-Label, Get-DueTone). 'now' is the local wall-clock time in 'tz'. JavaScript runs each",
    "group with TZ set to 'tz'; PowerShell's DateTime arithmetic has no time zone, so it takes 'now' as the wall clock.",
    "parse: [input, expected date or null, expected time ('' = none)]. A time alone means today, or tomorrow once it has",
    "passed on the wall clock. Weekday names mean the next one after today. A date without a year more than 30 days in",
    "the past means next year (and no date if that day does not exist then).",
    "labels: [date, expected label]. tones: [date, time, closed, expected 'over' | 'soon' | 'later' | 'closed']."
  ],
